Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:53:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] input: per-game HD Rumble intensity and weak rumble boost

hd_rumble_gain (25-1000 %) multiplies the amplitudes the game sends;
hd_rumble_low_boost (0-100 %) applies a power curve that lifts weak
vibrations more than strong ones, with a quadratic knee below 0.02 so
near-silent values do not turn into a constant buzz. Both are switchable,
so a game can carry its own values in its per-game config.

Some Switch 2 games never send amplitudes above 0.1: The Legend of Zelda:
Ocarina of Time (0400486024DEC000) peaks at 0.096 through command 214
(Mode 2), where Donkey Kong Bananza reaches 0.53. Gain 1000 % with
boost 60 % comes close to the console.

Feito com Claude Code
